        "original_id": "15e9254d-e2df-5ef0-8d36-27bb855945a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Plant, John Bonham, Phil Collins, Nika Boon, John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, Carey Willetts\n- Bands and Artists: Led Zeppelin, Massive Attack, Portishead, Kasabian, Pink Floyd, Mike Oldfield, Athlete\n- Roles: Drummer, Musician, Songwriter, Keyboardist, Guitarist, Bass player\n- Projects: Robert Plant tours, Nika Boon album\n\nFacts:\n- John Henry Bonham was born on 31 May 1948 and died on 25 September 1980.\n- John Bonham was an English musician and songwriter best known as the drummer for the British rock band Led Zeppelin.\n- Robert Plant avoided performing Led Zeppelin songs through much of that period.\n- Robert Plant's 1983 tour, with drummer Phil Collins, was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Robert Plant's 1985 tour was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Nika Boon was working on a new album planned for release in 2017.\n- Nika Boon's album involved collaboration with John Baggott, who played keyboard and moogs for Massive Attack, Portishead, and Robert Plant.\n- Nika Boon's album involved collaboration with Ian Matthews, the drummer from Kasabian, Jay Stapley, a guitarist associated with Pink Floyd and Mike Oldfield, and Carey Willetts, the bass player from Athlete.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
